Outage schedule data sources (read at runtime over public HTTP, not redistributed):

1. Lvivoblenergo (PrAT "Lvivoblenergo") open data
   - GPV schedule: https://api.loe.lviv.ua/api/menus?type=photo-grafic
   - Accidents by address: https://power-api.loe.lviv.ua/api/pw_accidents
   Data belongs to Lvivoblenergo.

2. YASNO public blackout-service API (Kyiv city, Dnipro DnEM / CEK)
   https://app.yasno.ua/api/blackout-service/public/shutdowns/...
   Data belongs to YASNO / DTEK Kyiv Electric Networks / DTEK Dnipro Electric Networks / CEK.

3. hukpo/ua-outages — https://github.com/hukpo/ua-outages
   Static aggregate https://hukpo.github.io/ua-outages/data/now.json of official operator
   schedules. Copyright (c) 2026 Pavlo Huk, MIT License. The compact data format
   (s: s/n/e/u, intervals [startMin, endMin, kind]) and region ids follow that project.
   Operator names in docs/MANUAL.md are taken from its now.json.

4. Oblenergo websites, read directly (server/oblenergo.py, android .../outage/OblenergoParsers.kt)
   - Kharkivoblenergo: https://oblenergo.kharkiv.ua/uk/jsonapi/node/newsforlenta (Drupal JSON:API)
   - Poltavaoblenergo: https://www.poe.pl.ua/customs/dynamicgpv-info.php
   - Zaporizhzhiaoblenergo: https://www.zoe.com.ua/outage/
   - Chernivtsioblenergo: https://oblenergo.cv.ua/shutdowns/
   Data belongs to each operator. The parsers are ported from hukpo/ua-outages
   (src/providers/{kharkiv,poltava,zaporizhzhia,chernivtsi}.ts and the shared helpers
   src/providers/posts.ts, src/providers/ua-text.ts, src/schedule.ts),
   Copyright (c) 2026 Pavlo Huk, MIT License — see the license text below.

5. Windows app (windows/) bundles these third-party components in its PyInstaller build:
   - pystray — LGPL-3.0-or-later (https://github.com/moses-palmer/pystray). It is shipped unmodified as
     a separate Python package inside the bundle (_internal); you may replace it with your own build.
   - Pillow — MIT-CMU (HPND) license (https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow)
   - pywebview — BSD-3-Clause (https://github.com/r0x0r/pywebview); pythonnet / clr_loader — MIT;
     bottle, proxy_tools — MIT (pywebview dependencies); Microsoft Edge WebView2 runtime is used
     from Windows, not redistributed
   - qrcode — BSD-3-Clause (https://github.com/lincolnloop/python-qrcode)
   - tzdata — Apache-2.0 (IANA time zone database is public domain)
   - CPython runtime — PSF License; PyInstaller bootloader — GPL-2.0 with the bootloader exception
   The installer is built with Inno Setup (https://jrsoftware.org/isinfo.php), which allows free use.

Each data source remains the property of its publisher; check their terms before heavy use.
The server polls every source at most once per 10 minutes with conditional requests
(ETag / If-Modified-Since) and an identifying User-Agent.

